CITARI OFFLINE KNOWLEDGE CATALOG — LICENSING & ATTRIBUTION NOTICE
==================================================================

This repository hosts unencrypted, Ed25519-signed offline knowledge packs and
catalog metadata built for Citari. Packs are compiled from multiple commercially
permissive open-knowledge sources. Each pack's exact license identifier, license
URL, snapshot date, and upstream source URL are embedded in both its
`manifest.json` and the `pack_meta` table of its `content.sqlite` database.

1. WIKIMEDIA PROJECTS (CC BY-SA 4.0)
------------------------------------
Packs derived from Wikimedia Foundation projects—including Simple English
Wikipedia (`en-wiki-top50k`), English Wikibooks (`en-wikibooks-guides`), English
Wikiversity (`en-wikiversity-cs`), and future Wikimedia packs (such as English
Wikipedia shards, Wikivoyage, Wiktionary, or Wikisource)—are licensed under the:

  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
  Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Under CC BY-SA 4.0, you are free to share (copy and redistribute the material in
any medium or format) and adapt (remix, transform, and build upon the material)
for any purpose, even commercially, provided you:
  - Give appropriate credit to the original authors/contributors (per-article
    `source_url` and `revision_id` are preserved in the `articles` table of
    `content.sqlite`, linking to each upstream page and its edit history),
    provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.
  - Distribute any adaptations under the same license (ShareAlike).
  - Do not apply legal terms or technological measures (DRM) that legally
    restrict others from doing anything the license permits.

Upstream dumps sourced from: https://dumps.wikimedia.org/

2. OTHER & FUTURE OPEN-LICENSED PACKS
-------------------------------------
Citari's pack pipeline enforces a fail-closed commercial-use allowlist. Future
packs added to this catalog may be distributed under one of the following
permissive licenses, as declared in each pack's `manifest.json` and `pack_meta`:

  - CC BY-SA 4.0 (e.g., Appropedia):
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  - CC BY-SA 2.5 (e.g., MDN Web Docs):
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5/
  - CC BY 4.0:
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  - CC0 1.0 Universal (Public Domain Dedication):
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
  - U.S. Federal Government Public Domain (17 U.S.C. § 105; federal .gov/.mil
    works only, excluding state/local works and copyrighted third-party material):
    https://www.usa.gov/government-copyright

3. SUMMARY OF MODIFICATIONS
---------------------------
All packs in this catalog are modified from their upstream source dumps as
follows:
  - Converted from source wikitext or documents to plain UTF-8 Markdown.
  - Infoboxes, tables, galleries, images, and reference footnotes were removed.
  - Articles flagged with copyright/non-free templates or categories, stub
    articles below the configured character threshold, and sub-article Fair Use
    blocks (<poem>, <score>, and lengthy verbatim quote templates) were stripped
    prior to indexing.
  - Remaining text was segmented into UTF-16 citation chunks, indexed with
    SQLite FTS5 and USearch HNSW vectors, and compressed with Zstd for offline
    search.

4. CATALOG METADATA & REPOSITORY DOCUMENTATION
----------------------------------------------
Original catalog metadata (`catalog.json`, `manifest.json`), signatures, and
documentation in this repository are dedicated to the public domain under
CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/), except
where third-party attribution notices apply.

